{"availability":"available","full":"autoatml/autoplex","name":"autoplex","description":"Code for automated fitting of machine learned interatomic potentials.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":162,"forks":28,"created":"2023-07-26T15:36:09Z","updated":"2026-10-09T08:17:25Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://autoatml.github.io/autoplex/","topics":["atomistic-machine-learning","atomistic-modelling","atomistic-simulations","high-throughput-computing","machine-learned-interatomic-potentials","ml-potentials","mlips"],"demo":"https://autoatml.github.io/autoplex/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:58:23.316Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:58:23.316Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:58:23.316Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:58.204Z","stars":162,"forks":28},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:49:15.839Z","stars":162,"forks":28},{"at":"2026-10-12T07:58:23.316Z","stars":162,"forks":28}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["autoplex is still under very active development and larger modifications to the source code should be expected.","autoplex is a software for generating and benchmarking machine learning (ML)-based interatomic potentials. The aim of autoplex is to provide a fully automated solution for creating high-quality ML potentials. The software is interfaced to multiple different ML potential fitting frameworks and to the atomate2 and ase environments for efficient high-throughput computations. The vision of this project is to allow a wide community of researchers to create accurate and reliable ML potentials for materials simulations.","autoplex is developed jointly by two research groups at BAM Berlin and the University of Oxford."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/autoatml/autoplex/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c54cb41eef2bd04b44b102dcf9cfdd5982fae0aa791760c722d99191efc8dd33","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:58.532Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-1